WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.680
 Photography is bigger
than just images.

00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:08.310
It's bigger than a career.

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:13.370
It's a process of discovery,
both external and internal.

00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:17.150
I want to invite you into
my world of photography.

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:18.950
Things aren't that
interesting for me

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.416
unless the stakes are very high.

00:00:21.416 --> 00:00:24.900
And we're going to scramble
to the top, top, top.

00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:27.520
With photography, you're
telling a narrative.

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.110
There's depth behind it--

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:33.010
one image to tell
this whole story.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.380
Think about how they
look visually, what

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:37.930
your compositions look like.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:41.030
The way I'm shooting this,
I'm underexposing quite a bit.

00:00:41.030 --> 00:00:43.980
I know that I'm going to
pull up the shadows in post.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:48.340
All of a sudden, it changes the
entire dynamic of the image.

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:51.445
It really begins before
you even pick up a camera.

00:00:51.445 --> 00:00:53.070
When you're passionate
about something,

00:00:53.070 --> 00:00:55.620
you know something deeply.

00:00:55.620 --> 00:00:57.830
It takes obsessiveness.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:00.610
It should be a calling.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.342
Oh, god.

00:01:02.342 --> 00:01:05.168
[LAUGHS]

00:01:05.168 --> 00:01:07.994
The best types of shoots are the
ones where you're having fun.

00:01:07.994 --> 00:01:08.936
[LAUGHS]

00:01:08.936 --> 00:01:10.570
I think I'm going to
go a little lower.

00:01:10.570 --> 00:01:12.850
I want him higher
in the horizon line.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.190
And you build incredible
relationships.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:16.900
Some images are
impossible unless you

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.430
have that relationship.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.540
That's great, Conrad.

00:01:19.540 --> 00:01:22.180
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.010
What I've realized
over the years

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:26.560
is there's always going
to be the next big thing.

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:30.420
Appreciate being in the
moment with what you're doing.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.330
Photography is
such a cool vehicle

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:36.130
to give you access to the world.

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:40.900
Look at where the bar has been
set before and set it higher.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.756
Ask yourself what you're
willing to do to get there.

00:01:43.756 --> 00:01:46.930
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:51.260
I'm Jimmy Chin, and
this is my MasterClass.

